    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Hey, i'm looking at a contract for a shipment of electronic components coming from South Korea to Germany. It says CIF. can you explain exactly what the seller is responsible for under CIF Incoterms 2020?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Under CIF Incoterms 2020, the seller is responsible for the costs and risks of the goods up to the port of destination in Germany, including international freight and insurance. However, this is not true \"delivery to destination\"; the risk of loss or damage to the goods actually transfers to the buyer once the goods are on board the vessel in South Korea. Consequently, the seller must arrange and pay for the main carriage insurance, but the buyer bears all risks from that point forward, apart from paying the remaining freight and insurance if they are not fully detailed in the CIF terms.",
      "source": "target",
