    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "ok thanks. just to clarify, if the shipment gets damaged while it's actually on the water—like, during the transit from korea to germany—who handles the insurance claim process? and does the seller have to provide the insurance policy to the buyer?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Since the risk transfers to the buyer once the goods are on board the vessel in South Korea, the buyer is legally entitled to make a claim against the insurer for goods damaged at sea. Under CIF Incoterms 2020, the seller is required to obtain a minimum coverage insurance policy, and they must provide a verified copy of the insurance document along with the original bill of lading to the buyer. The buyer then uses this policy to file the claim, though in practice, the seller often advises the buyer on the procedure to ensure they can recover the loss.",
      "source": "target",
