    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "got it. one more thing—the contract mentions \"minimum coverage.\" does the seller have any discretion over which insurance provider they use, or are there specific requirements for the type of coverage they have to provide for these electronics?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Under CIF, the seller generally selects the insurance provider but must ensure the policy meets ISO Commercial General Clause \"A\" (All Risks), which covers electronic components broadly but can have specific exclusions like war or strike that the seller still needs to cover or exclude. However, the seller cannot alter the core \"minimum coverage\" level; if the goods are damaged by peril covered under Clause A, the carrier and insurer will typically compensate for the loss up to the insured value. This requirement is standard across trade unless your specific contract or local German law imposes additional, stricter insurance mandates.",
      "source": "target",
